~ start
You: You're let into the Headmaster's office by a prim secretary. The Headmaster waves you to a seat and gives you a long look and a slow nod. The office is all warm wood and dark velvet, luxuriously appointed from the chandelier to the carpet. The Headmaster is younger than you expected - his hair is merely graying, not white. He's trimly dressed in a comfortable-looking suit.
Headmaster: "You must be the one Gelee talked about." He waves to the desk, where a pile of your research sits. "I had a look through the papers you sent over. They're clever and insightful." He rubs his chin. "But you want to learn more magic." It's not really a question, and you both know it.
~ Mid
- "Who is Gelee anyways?" \n Ask about the Butterfly Maiden. 
	Headmaster: "Gelee is one of the Queen's... handmaidens. Or that's what they call themselves; they're more like a secret police. But different from the King's secret police." He snorts. "Politics is a fools game, y'hear?" He shakes his head firmly. "You can trust her to keep her word, but don't go making her mad." => Mid
- "Can I learn magic here?" \n It's why you came.
	Headmaster: "I'm honestly not sure if we have anyone qualified to teach you - but if you've demonstrated one thing," he nods to your research, "it's your ability to learn on your own. If you're interested in abstruse magic, we have examples you can study. We just need to work out payment..." => Mid
	Headmaster: "We have several relics, left behind by mages of yore. We can give you access to study them, for university credits."
- "What magic can you teach?" \n Hopefully a new one...
	Headmaster: "Ah, types, right... Well. There's the Malachite Hive, which we believe might be a relic of an Apimancer, a mage who worked with bees."
	Headmaster: "There's the Clockwork Isle, which we believe belonged to an Ergomancer, a mage who studied energies at work."
	Headmaster: "And there's the Skybound Alembic, which we know belonged to a Calcimancer, a famous alchemist who's estate donated it to us." => Mid
- "Gelee mentioned a trade..." \n Of course it's not free.
	Headmaster: "That's right. Your research on mirrors... Mirrormancy, you called it? Absolutely faascinating. If you'd be willing to teach a class on that, or even just deliver a few lectures, I'm sure we could find you some interesting spells to study. Oneiromancy and thalassomancy as well, they're exotic enough." => Mid
- "Alright, I'll be around, then." \n You'll think it over.
=> END